{
  "title": "Insta360 GO Ultra mount: latch base, hinged cage, GoPro prongs and cold shoe",
  "summary": "An all-purpose mount for the GO Ultra in its Action Pod: two printed hooks click into the pod's own latch slots, a rigid cage with a hinged top bar holds it in every direction and keeps the flip screen and every control free, GoPro-standard prongs underneath take helmet, chest and bike mounts, and a cold-shoe adapter puts it on a camera or a rig.",
  "status": "preview",
  "date": "2026-11-26",
  "material": "PLA test print on TNT (PETG later for action use); TPU 95A fin pads on Gås. Bought: M5 x 25-30 hex bolt + M5 nut; 1.75 mm filament for pins.",
  "notes": "Iteration 4, after four review rounds by independent reviewers (functionality, durability, ergonomics, aesthetics; all PASS, PETG pending its physical tests). How it holds: the pod sits on the base; a hinged bar across the front of the top clamps it through two TPU fin pads (2.4 N, takes up +-0.45 mm of height); two hooks on PLA flexures catch the pod's latch slots and carry no load while the bar is closed; two 4 mm end frames (0.4 mm from the pod, pinned dovetail feet) stop it sideways. Nothing fixed sits over the pod, so with the bar open it lifts straight out. Open: thumb on the bar, push the tab above the camera-end frame outward (5 N), lift the bar. Remove: squeeze both end buttons (6 N), lift by the two notches in the base. Screen panel and flip path, shutter, power, Q, USB-C (with a plug), release switch, speakers, mics, lights and the lens view (80 deg half-angle) are all kept clear. GoPro-standard 2 prongs (13 mm under the base: 25 mm thumbscrews fit). Cold-shoe stack: printed 3-prong head, two foot widths, lock wheel; real M5 bolt and nut (printed M5 threads were too fine). verify_mount.py: 103 checks, 0 fail; open items need the real camera: latch-hole depth (hook tip 4.3 mm in), rim thickness, slot position, lens glass position, camera top height, shutter position (one parameter each). Print the base alone first (44 min) as the fit test. Infill: functional, 6 walls, 60 % gyroid, 0.12 mm layers; TNT at 230 C / 12 mm3/s. For helmet/bike use: PETG version (GO_ULTRA_MAT=PETG: thicker flexures and snap, 2 mm steel hinge pin), its physical tests first, and tie the safety cord to the helmet.",
